  "outcome": {
    "ok": true,
    "turn_id": "d09_final_matched:r4:t3",
    "narration": "Iris waited a beat after the question, her gaze moving across the open floor toward the perimeter where the spiral stair arrived. She seemed to consider it genuinely rather than out of politeness.\n\n\"Quiet, I think,\" she said. Then, after that familiar pause: \"At least for now.\"\n\nShe settled on one of the simple stools beside the nearer bed, the one closest to the stair's edge. The floor above was spare and still — two empty beds with their bare frames, the matching stools and nightstands, the tall wardrobes standing shut against the wall, and across from them the closed faces of the medical-storage cabinets. Nothing in any of them yet. Late daylight came through the tower's stone openings and lay in pale strips across the floor, picking out dust motes and the grain of the wood. From somewhere below, faintly, the sounds of the ground floor — whatever the lower room held — barely reached up through the open stairwell, distant enough to ignore.",
